{"name":"Purple Protégé","hex":"#593569","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"protégé","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is guided and supported by an older and more experienced person (a protector or mentor)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prot%C3%A9g%C3%A9"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mentorship","blocks":[{"text":"Mentorship is the patronage, influence, guidance, or direction given by a mentor. A mentor is someone who teaches or gives help and advice to a less experienced and often younger person. In an organizational setting, a mentor influences the personal and professional growth of a mentee. Most traditional mentorships involve having senior employees mentor more junior employees, but mentors do not necessarily have to be more senior than the people they mentor. What matters is that mentors have experience that others can learn from."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/US_Army_52782_Mentoring_the_next_generation.jpg/330px-US_Army_52782_Mentoring_the_next_generation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mentorship"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Age_Teaching_Youth.jpg/500px-Age_Teaching_Youth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Age_Teaching_Youth.jpg/500px-Age_Teaching_Youth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"William Blake's \"Age Teaching Youth\", a Romantic image of mentorship[15]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAge_Teaching_Youth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg/500px-Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg/1280px-Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg/500px-Senior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A senior editor mentors a junior editor.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASenior_editor_mentoring_junior_editor.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/